OL,3,ABritish man infected with Ebola in DR
OL,4,ACongo arrives in UK for treatment
OL,5,
OL,6,FA British man who tested positive for
OL,7,FEbola in the Democratic Republic of
OL,8,FCongo has been flown back to the UK.
OL,10,FThe man, who is a health worker and has
OL,11,Fnot been identified, landed at RAF
OL,12,FNortholt before being transported to a
OL,13,Fspecialist infectious diseases unit at
OL,14,Fthe Royal Free Hospital in north
OL,15,FLondon.
OL,17,FIt is the first confirmed case of a UK
OL,18,Fnational contracting Ebola during the
OL,19,Fmost recent outbreak of the rare but
OL,20,Fdeadly virus in DR Congo, which has so
OL,21,Ffar led to more than 5,000 deaths.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,308,300,200,140,0,100
